# With word wrap on, Ctrl+D moves about one screenful, so the block just below the first page is still on screen.
size 50 14
config <<END
word_wrap = true
END
file <<END
Long list:
	- Item 01 is a task with a fairly long description that will wrap
	- Item 02 is a task with a fairly long description that will wrap
	- Item 03 is a task with a fairly long description that will wrap
	- Item 04 is a task with a fairly long description that will wrap
	- Item 05 is a task with a fairly long description that will wrap
	- Item 06 is a task with a fairly long description that will wrap
	- Item 07 is a task with a fairly long description that will wrap
	- Item 08 is a task with a fairly long description that will wrap
	- Item 09 is a task with a fairly long description that will wrap
	- Item 10 is a task with a fairly long description that will wrap
	- Item 11 is a task with a fairly long description that will wrap
	- Item 12 is a task with a fairly long description that will wrap
	- Item 13 is a task with a fairly long description that will wrap
	- Item 14 is a task with a fairly long description that will wrap
	- Item 15 is a task with a fairly long description that will wrap
	- Item 16 is a task with a fairly long description that will wrap
	- Item 17 is a task with a fairly long description that will wrap
	- Item 18 is a task with a fairly long description that will wrap
	- Item 19 is a task with a fairly long description that will wrap
	- Item 20 is a task with a fairly long description that will wrap
	- Item 21 is a task with a fairly long description that will wrap
	- Item 22 is a task with a fairly long description that will wrap
	- Item 23 is a task with a fairly long description that will wrap
	- Item 24 is a task with a fairly long description that will wrap
	- Item 25 is a task with a fairly long description that will wrap
END
see - Item 05 is a task
hide - Item 06 is a task
keys <C-d>
see - Item 06 is a task
quit
